🔹 🎯 Task 1: Array of Objects and Static Field

You are building a Student registry that tracks students with a static counter.

📥 Input:
String[] names;
int[] ages;

⚙️ Requirements:
• Create a Student class with:
  - Private fields: name (String), age (int)
  - Static field: totalStudents (int, initialized to 0)
  - Constructor Student(String name, int age) that increments totalStudents
  - Method info() that returns "Student{name='<name>', age=<age>}"
  - Static method getTotalStudents() that returns totalStudents
• In main(), create an array of 4 Student objects
• Print each student's info
• Print the total student count using the static method

⚠️ Watch out:
• Static fields are shared across ALL instances — they don't get reset when you create a new object. Each constructor call increments the same counter.
• In JS, you'd use a WeakMap or closure to track instances. In Java, use a static field — it lives in metaspace, not on the heap per object.
• Array initialization: Student[] students = new Student[4] creates the array, but you must still call new Student(...) for each element.

📤 Output format:
Student{name='<name1>', age=<age1>}
Student{name='<name2>', age=<age2>}
Student{name='<name3>', age=<age3>}
Student{name='<name4>', age=<age4>}
Total students: 4

