🔹 🎯 Task 2: Inheritance and Method Override

You are building a shape hierarchy where Circle and Rectangle inherit from Shape.

📥 Input:
double radius (for Circle);
double length, width (for Rectangle);

⚙️ Requirements:
• Create a Shape class with:
  - Protected field: name (String)
  - Method getArea() that returns 0.0
  - Method describe() that prints "Shape: <name>"
• Create Circle class extending Shape with:
  - Private field: radius
  - Constructor Circle(double radius) that sets name to "Circle"
  - Override getArea() to return π * radius²
• Create Rectangle class extending Shape with:
  - Private fields: length, width
  - Constructor Rectangle(double length, double width) that sets name to "Rectangle"
  - Override getArea() to return length * width
• In main(), create one Circle and one Rectangle, call describe() on each, then print their areas

⚠️ Watch out:
• In JS, you'd prototype chain; in Java, you use extends and override methods. The child class can call super() implicitly or explicitly.
• Math.PI is a static final constant in Java — use Math.PI, not M_PI or similar.
• Polymorphism: describe() is inherited from Shape but works on both Circle and Rectangle without casting.

📤 Output format:
Shape: Circle
Shape: Rectangle
Circle area: X.XX
Rectangle area: X.XX

